# Vanessa Automation Run Policy

> When a run is mandatory: creating/modifying `.feature`, launch parameters, or `bddRunner.epf`.

## MUST

| Requirement | Description |
|------------|----------|
| Mandatory run | After modifying a scenario agent MUST execute the scenario run |
| Mandatory artifact analysis | After the run agent MUST check `va-status.json` and `vanessa-execution.log` |
| Mandatory event log analysis | After the run agent MUST check `event-log` if the scenario failed or the run looks suspicious |
| Explicit classification | On failure agent MUST return an error class rather than just failure text |

## Sign of success

Minimum sign of success:

1. the `va-status.json` file exists;
2. the value in `va-status.json` equals `0`;
3. the `vanessa-execution.log` file was created.

The detailed execution and diagnostics procedure is described by the skills, not by this rule.

